# Coverage of the `codex` CLI, 0.165.0 (specs/047). Format and rules: crates/delphi-engine/src/coverage.rs.
# S1 (read-only `exec --json` seats) uses the rows marked `used`; the rest wait for their slice.
# kind | path | names | disposition | slice | reason

# ── Flags that appear on several pages: one disposition wherever they appear ──
flag | * | --help, --version | na | | every CLI prints its help and version
flag | * | --config | used | | `-c key=value` only from a short allow-list, and so far only `model_reasoning_effort` (from `effort`) and `features.shell_tool=false` (a reader seat has no shell: the read-only sandbox still reads any file on disk, probed 2026-10-28); any other key could widen authority, so it is refused
flag | * | --enable, --disable | refused | | flips a feature flag, which could turn on surface Delphi has not classified
flag | * | --strict-config | na | | the operator's config is ignored (`--ignore-user-config`), so there is nothing to be strict about
flag | * | --model | used | | the span's model
flag | * | --sandbox | used | | `read-only` for every S1 seat; `workspace-write` for a Builder in its worktree only once the approval bridge is proven; `danger-full-access` refused
flag | * | --cd | na | | the process is started in the span's directory instead
flag | * | --add-dir | planned | S2 | only for a span with tools, from the ratified block (as spec 021)
flag | * | --ask-for-approval | planned | S2 | `never` for a reader; `on-request` once the app-server bridge answers the requests
flag | * | --image | planned | S3 | vision, off by default
flag | * | --search | planned | S3 | live web search; ratified, off by default, results untrusted (spec 020)
flag | * | --no-daemon | planned | S2 | not a flag of `exec` (0.165.0); S2 decides whether the commands that have it (introspection) must pass it so they never attach to the operator's shared background server
flag | * | --approve-for-me | refused | | routes approvals to the CLI's own automatic reviewer; Delphi's approvals stay Delphi's (spec 047 §1.1)
flag | * | --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox, --dangerously-bypass-hook-trust | refused | | skips approvals, sandbox or hook trust; never passed
flag | * | --profile | refused | | layers the operator's own config file over the span's
flag | * | --oss, --local-provider | refused | | the local-model route; Delphi has `family = "local"`
flag | * | --worktree | refused | | Delphi owns worktrees (specs 003, 008)
flag | * | --remote, --remote-auth-token-env | refused | | connects to a remote app server outside Delphi's
flag | * | --no-alt-screen | na | | interactive display

# ── Top level and `exec` ──
cmd | . | exec | planned | S1 | `codex exec --json` for read-only roles, structured output, API-key mode
flag | exec | --json, --output-schema, --ephemeral, --ignore-user-config, --skip-git-repo-check | used | | the span's launch (spec 047 §2.2): events on stdout, the schema written to a scratch file, nothing persisted, the operator's config ignored, a git check skipped only in Delphi's scratch directory
flag | exec | --output-last-message | na | | the final message arrives as a JSON event on stdout
flag | exec | --ignore-rules | refused | | skips the user's execpolicy rules, a safety layer
flag | exec | --cyber-access-program | refused | | requests an experimental access program
flag | exec | --color, --thread-source | na | | display, thread classification
cmd | exec | resume, fork | planned | S1 | resume or fork by id; --last and --all are refused (directory-dependent)
cmd | exec | review | planned | S3 | a cheap read-only review lane
cmd | . | review | planned | S3 | as `exec review`
flag | review | --uncommitted, --base, --commit, --title | planned | S3 | the review target

# ── Commands that change global state or the account ──
cmd | . | logout, update | operator-only | | changes stored credentials or the installed CLI
cmd | . | migrate-rollouts, migrate-nfs-db | operator-only | | migrates the operator's saved sessions or databases

group | login | | operator-only | | signs in (ChatGPT, API key, access token, device code)
cmd | login | status | read-only | S2 | exit 0 when credentials exist; doctor's login check

group | mcp | | operator-only | | writes ~/.codex/config.toml
cmd | mcp | list, get | read-only | S2 | the configured servers

group | plugin | | operator-only | | installs or removes plugins and marketplaces
cmd | plugin | list | read-only | S2 | `--json`

group | features | | operator-only | | writes feature flags in config.toml
cmd | features | list | read-only | S2 | the feature flags and their state

# ── Read-only diagnostics ──
cmd | . | doctor | read-only | S2 | summarized in `delphi doctor`
group | debug | | na | | developer tooling
cmd | debug | models | read-only | S2 | the account's model catalog as JSON; feeds tier discovery as `agy models` does
cmd | debug | prompt-input | read-only | S2 | the model-visible prompt, to prove Delphi's governance text arrives

# ── The approval bridge ──
group | app-server | | used | | the bidirectional JSON-RPC protocol that answers approval requests like Claude's permission-prompt-tool (`Opts.app_server`, specs/047 S2b); experimental, probed on 0.165.0, and a protocol change fails the stand-in and live tests rather than a span silently
flag | app-server | --stdio | used | | stdio only: no listener on a port or socket
flag | app-server | --listen | refused | | a listener on a port or socket
flag | app-server | --ws-audience, --ws-auth, --ws-issuer, --ws-max-clock-skew-seconds, --ws-shared-secret-file, --ws-token-file, --ws-token-sha256 | refused | | websocket listener authentication; Delphi uses stdio
flag | app-server | --analytics-default-enabled, --cloud-skills-snapshot, --code-mode-host, --print-startup-config, --startup-client-info, --startup-sign-out | refused | | reaches the vendor's cloud or changes the account's state
cmd | app-server | generate-json-schema, generate-ts | read-only | S2 | emit the protocol's schema; S2 records it in the snapshot to detect protocol drift
cmd | app-server | daemon, proxy | refused | | a long-running server outside Delphi's daemon

# ── Refused: the vendor's cloud, remote sessions, session management ──
cmd | . | agents, queue, archive, unarchive, delete, resume, fork, apply, app, exec-server | refused | | manages the vendor's sessions, applies a cloud diff, opens the desktop app, or runs a server outside Delphi's
group | cloud | | refused | | hands work to OpenAI's infrastructure
group | remote-control | | refused | | leaves a session running outside the daemon
cmd | . | completion | na | | shell completion
group | sandbox | | na | | runs a command under Codex's own sandbox; Delphi has its own sandbox crate
